            <ArticleTitle>Delirium as a contributing factor to &quot;crescendo&quot; pain: three case reports.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cancer patients occasionally experience periods of rapidly escalating pain--&quot;crescendo&quot; pain--that may present a challenge in assessment and management. Although these episodes are often associated with progressive neoplasm, any of a variety of other processes may be involved. Delirium is a potentially treatable and frequently unrecognized factor. We present three patients who illustrate this relationship between delirium and a crescendo pattern of cancer pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
